iguration. It is working perfectly for the specific paths. Removing the * does not help. It seems as if specifing a root path is not working.\r\n\r\nquarkus.keycloak.policy-enforcer.enable=true\r\n\r\nquarkus.keycloak.policy-enforcer.paths.1.name=Root\r\nquarkus.keycloak.policy-enforcer.paths.1.path=/*\r\nquarkus.keycloak.policy-enforcer.paths.1.enforcement-mode=DISABLED\r\n\r\nquarkus.keycloak.policy-enforcer.paths.2.name=API\r\nquarkus.keycloak.policy-enforcer.paths.2.path=/api/*\r\nquarkus.keycloak.policy-enforcer.paths.2.enforcement-mode=ENFORCING\r\n\r\nquarkus.keycloak.policy-enforcer.paths.3.name=Public\r\nquarkus.keycloak.policy-enforcer.paths.3.path=/hello\r\nquarkus.keycloak.policy-enforcer.paths.3.enforcement-mode=DISABLED\r\n\r\n**Expected behavior**\r\nEverything that is not at /api should be accessable anonymously.\r\n\r\n**Actual behavior**\r\n/hello is, but / is not.\r\n\r\n**To Reproduce**\r\n1. Following the keycloak-integration example at quarkus.io \r\n2. Use the application.properties from above\r\n3. Try to access / without a valid Bearer-Token\r\n```\r\n\r\n**Environment (please complete the following information):**\r\n - Output of `uname -a` or `ver`: Windows 10 \r\n - Output of `java -version`: OpenJDK 11\r\n - GraalVM version (if different from Java): n/a\r\n - Quarkus version or git rev: 1.2.1\r\n - Build tool (ie. output of `mvnw --version` or `gradlew --version`): Apache Maven 3.6.3","closed_by":{"login":"sberyozkin","id":467639,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2NzYzOQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/467639?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sberyozkin","html_url":"https://github.com/sberyozkin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sberyozkin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sberyozkin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sberyozkin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sberyozkin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptio